Hash each case under its own strategy, and skip ignored cases (applied by relative_oracle.py after A0)

Upstream added `TestCase.ignore` and per-case specialization strategies
(the "(specialize=no)" variants run under `.boxy`). A0's hash mode
compiled every case under the default `.lss` and hashed ignored cases
too. On 2026-11-26 upstream ignored "issue 11698: curried lambdas" under
`.lss` until upstream issue 13560 (`30ed9367ab`); compiling it under `.lss`
grows without bound, and hash mode compiled both it and its `.boxy`
variant that way, so the oracle ran out of memory (27 GB) on every side.
`devObjectHashes` now takes the case's strategy for publishing and
lowering, and `devCodeHashApplies` skips a case the runners ignore
(`TestCase.isIgnored`). Applies after 0004-runtime-requests-items.patch.

